ion whatever; I have distinguished no creature besides, of all the numbers resorting hither, except Sir James Martin, on whom I bestowed a little notice, in order to detach him from M…”"},{"id":"de-courcy","name":"De Courcy","aliases":["Mr. De Courcy","Lady De Courcy"],"role":"major","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: “Vernon to Lady De Courcy._”"},{"id":"mr-vernon","name":"Mr. Vernon","role":"major","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “_Lady Susan Vernon to Mr.”"},{"id":"mrs-vernon","name":"Mrs. Vernon","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “MY DEAR BROTHER,—I can no longer refuse myself the pleasure of profiting by your kind invitation when we last parted of spending some weeks with you at Churchhill, and, therefore, if quite convenient to you and Mrs.”"},{"id":"mr-johnson","name":"Mr. Johnson","role":"supporting","group":"g-johnson","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “If I am as little in favour with Mr.”"},{"id":"mrs-johnson","name":"Mrs. Johnson","role":"supporting","group":"g-johnson","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “_Lady Susan Vernon to Mrs.”"},{"id":"mrs-mainwaring","name":"Mrs. Mainwaring","role":"supporting","group":"g-mainwaring","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “The event of all this is very provoking: Sir James is gone, Maria highly incensed, and Mrs.”"},{"id":"alicia","name":"Alicia","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “You were mistaken, my dear Alicia, in supposing me fixed at this place for the rest of the winter: it grieves me to say how greatly you were mistaken, for I have seldom spent three months more agreeably than those whi…”"},{"id":"catherine","name":"Catherine","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s11","summary":"First mention: “Charles Vernon, and yet, in spite of his generous endeavours to excuse her, we know that she did, from the most selfish motives, take all possible pains to prevent his marriage with Catherine.”"},{"id":"miss-mainwaring","name":"Miss Mainwaring","role":"supporting","group":"g-mainwaring","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “I have avoided all general flirtation whatever; I have distinguished no creature besides, of all the numbers resorting hither, except Sir James Martin, on whom I bestowed a little notice, in order to detach him from M…”"},{"id":"charles-vernon","name":"Charles Vernon","aliases":["Charles"],"role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “Charles Vernon is my aversion; and I am afraid of his wife.”"},{"id":"miss-summers","name":"Miss Summers","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “My young lady accompanies me to town, where I shall deposit her under the care of Miss Summers, in Wigmore street, till she becomes a little more reasonable.”"},{"id":"miss-vernon","name":"Miss Vernon","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: “Miss Vernon is to be placed at a school in London before her mother comes to us which I am glad of, for her sake and my own.”"},{"id":"mr-smith","name":"Mr. Smith","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s4","summary":"First mention: “I learnt all this from Mr.”"}],"relationships":[{"id":"r1","source":"mr-vernon","target":"susan-vernon","weight":15,"phases":[{"at":"s1","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":1,"note":"First named together in Ch. 1."},{"at":"s35","type":"together","label":"Often together","weight":13}]},{"id":"r2","source":"mrs-johnson","target":"susan-vernon","weight":14,"phases":[{"at":"s2","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":1,"note":"First named together in Ch. 2."},{"at":"s29","type":"together","label":"Often together","weight":12}]},{"id":"r3","source":"alicia","target":"sir-james-martin","weight":5,"phases":[{"at":"s2","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":1,"note":"First named together in Ch. 2."}]},{"id":"r4","source":"alicia","target":"frederica","w